<item>
            <title>[LU-20600] osp: cannot tell when object precreation stopped or resumed on an OST</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20600</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;An MDS stops precreating objects on an OST when the free space reported by that OST drops below osp.&lt;b&gt;.reserved_mb_low, or its free inode count drops below osp.&lt;/b&gt;.reserved_ino_low, and resumes only once the corresponding *_high watermark is crossed back.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both transitions are only reported at CDEBUG(D_INFO) level, so in practice an administrator cannot see them. &#160;osp.*.prealloc_status reports the current state alone: polling it tells neither when a transition happened,&lt;br/&gt;
nor which free space or free inode value triggered it, nor which watermark that value was compared against. &#160;Once the OST has recovered, there is no way to tell that it was ever out of space, or for how long.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raising the two edges to console warnings was considered first, but it does not scale &amp;#8211; a setup with hundreds or thousands of OSTs would flood the logs in corner cases, so it would have to be optional at the very least.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What is needed is a way to see, per OST, when precreation last stopped and resumed and what values caused it, without adding anything to the logs.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
